Construction drawings usually require tracking and management.

He needs to submit the Shop Drawing to us. In practice, there is a Transmittal document, and after our review, another Transmittal is generated as a record. Additionally, some Shop Drawings require not only our review but also approval by the client or other relevant disciplines. For example, generator equipment involving mechanical systems, including fuel or natural gas pipelines, also requires our participation in the review.

The revision and review log of Shop Drawings are crucial. The review log meticulously records details of each Shop Drawing, including equipment type, submission date, reviewers, review outcomes, and subsequent revision reviews. These elements form the complete project documentation.
